    <briefdescription>
<para>Deprecated concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework floating-point wrapper with a tolerance. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>has_epsilon</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a framework expression type (see <computeroutput>is_op</computeroutput>) with an <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput> member, like <computeroutput>floating_point_constant</computeroutput> and the floating-point specialisation of <computeroutput>value&lt;T&gt;</computeroutput>. The comparators treat the operands within this tolerance as equal; a custom comparator uses it to do the same.</para>
<para>The types of the application are excluded, even if they have a member named <computeroutput>epsilon</computeroutput>, so that they are compared with their own operators.</para>
<para>Only the deprecated floating-point wrappers have a tolerance, so the concept is deprecated with them, and is available only when <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-config_1ga67c701de5426ac340584ed038494a873" kindref="member">MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED</ref></computeroutput> is defined.</para>
<para><xrefsect id="deprecated_1_deprecated000117"><xreftitle>Deprecated</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>to be removed with the deprecated floating-point wrappers (since 6.0.0) </para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
